  "body": "As discussed in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=654072 it might be good to have more alignment about what form restoration entails. Questions that came up:\r\n\r\n* Is disabled restorable state?\r\n* Should restoration happen on \"soft\" reload?\r\n* Should there be an event? It sounds like `pageshow` might be good enough for this, provided things are restored at that time. As noted in #7283 it seems developers could also use `formStateRestoreCallback` for this, which makes it very observable when exactly this process takes place...\r\n\r\nFurther context: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6853#issuecomment-951012997.\r\n\r\ncc @gijsk @whatwg/forms ",
